When using the provided [json.gbnf](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/blob/master/grammars/json.gbnf) with the llamap.cpp library API I permanently get 

<Sampler/grammar exception: Unexpected empty grammar stack after accepting piece: {"

I use a self-trained gemma3b-it-270m model and I have confirmed that my trained model emits proper JSON like ` {"intent":"power_off"}`. I also tried my own grammar, but I get the same issue. The most simple one which works so far, is:

~~~bnf
root ::= ws "{" any-content "}" ws

# Match any character sequence (including quotes and backslashes)
any-content ::= .*

# Whitespace (spaces, tabs, newlines)
ws ::= ([ \t\n\r])*
~~~

But this does still allow invalid JSON.

