### Problem description & steps to reproduce

Related: #26540 (closed automatically for inactivity).

A continuously rotating CSS spinner reduces local CUDA generation throughput even on a standalone page without llama-ui, Svelte, or Markdown. In bundled llama-ui, stopping only the loading spinner improved throughput from about 42 to 52.82 tokens/s.

### Environment and limitations

Windows 10 Pro; i7-11800H; 32GB RAM; RTX 3070 Laptop 8GB; NVIDIA driver 610.62; Codex in-app Chromium browser. Backend/model/version and flags are listed above. **Not reproduced on current upstream, standalone Chrome/Edge, or another OS yet.** This may involve browser/GPU scheduling or resource contention; the exact mechanism and whether upstream is affected remain unconfirmed.

### Measurements

Each case uses the same prompt, seed 42, 384 output tokens, thinking disabled, and cache_prompt=false. Cases run sequentially. Speeds are backend timings.predicted_per_second, not browser paint timing. These are single runs with a repeated baseline, not a statistical benchmark.

| Rendering mode | Backend tokens/s |
| --- | ---: |
| Consume SSE without output updates | 59.40 |
| Only a 20px rotating CSS spinner | 44.95 |
| Plain text update per event, no spinner | 54.06 |
| Plain text update at most every 100ms, no spinner | 58.75 |
| Plain text per event plus spinner | 44.08 |
| Repeat no-output baseline | 57.95 |

In actual llama-ui, applying `.loading-icon.animate-spin { animation: none !important; }` via Custom CSS yielded 52.82 tokens/s over 720 tokens with normal text streaming. Computed animation-name was verified as none; console had no warnings/errors. The rotating Loader2 is in tools/ui/src/lib/components/app/chat/ChatTabs/ChatTabsItem.svelte in the tested revision.

